    {
     "field": "plain_english",
     "severity": "High",
     "issue": "plain_english (and purpose_function/practical_application) describe a home-theater AV receiver's dedicated sub output and receiver-based bass management, but the definition defines the term as a live-sound technique of driving subs from a console aux send fed by selected LF channels. The fields contradict the definition, so a reader cannot tell what 'aux-fed subwoofer' actually means.",
     "suggestion": "Rewrite plain_english (and align purpose_function/practical_application) to the definition's live-sound sense, e.g.: 'Instead of letting the subs take the full main mix, you feed them from a dedicated aux send and choose exactly which low-frequency channels go to it - typically kick, bass, toms, and synths. This gives the engineer channel-by-channel control over what reaches the subs and keeps other sources out of them.'"
